tence and cron service recovery.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/cron package/service and confirmed no /etc/cron.allow or /etc/cron.deny existed, and opsadmin user did not exist\",\"Created opsadmin user (locked password, home dir) on node1\",\"Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing exactly 'root' and 'opsadmin', root:root owned, mode 644; removed any stray /etc/cron.deny\",\"Verified root and opsadmin can use crontab (list and install a job), then cleaned up the test job\",\"Created and used a throwaway low-priv test user to confirm crontab denies non-listed users, then deleted that test user\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and cron/cron.allow/opsadmin state as baseline\",\"Issued a native reboot on node1 (single node) with acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart: cron service active, /etc/cron.allow and opsadmin persisted, opsadmin allowed, a fresh ephemeral test user denied, then removed that test user\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: no pre-existing cron.allow/cron.deny, opsadmin absent\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-97a26faa3e8a40f3\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed /etc/cron.allow and /etc/cron.deny did not exist and opsadmin user did not exist prior to changes\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-277f88d872df42bd\",\"cmd-7db37a932bf1403e\"],\"summary\":\"Created /etc/cron.allow with root and opsadmin; demonstrated root and opsadmin can use crontab (list/install job) while a non-listed test user (crontest) is explicitly denied with 'You (crontest) are not allowed to use this program (crontab)'; cleaned up test user and temp job\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + service health) for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c1f2c0009ce34831\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id f9bf293d-1eb8-423e-b185-84e94db646f3, cron service active, cron.allow contents, and opsadmin existence before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-47a4b27c28c94cd9\"],\"summary\":\"Issued native 'reboot' via backgrounded sudo command; 'reboot-acknowledged' returned to the caller before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof of actual restart via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8070961b414649b2\",\"cmd-3c66ada1cbf744d3\"],\"summary\":\"Connection reset confirmed the node went down; subsequent poll succeeded with boot_id changed to 72810ce8-b39f-4307-a33a-450cd2387bf3 and new uptime, proving a real reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of cron service, cron.allow restriction, and opsadmin account\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8f6f813b43564c24\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, cron service active, /etc/cron.allow still contains root/opsadmin, opsadmin account persists and can use crontab, and a freshly created ephemeral test user is still denied by crontab (then removed), confirming the restriction survived the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, cron scheduling is now restricted to root and opsadmin via /etc/cron.allow. opsadmin user was created (did not previously exist). Verified via a throwaway test user that non-listed users are denied by crontab, and that opsadmin/root are permitted, both before and after a full node restart (boot_id changed from f9bf293d... to 72810ce8...), confirming persistence and cron service recovery.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/cron package/service and confirmed no /etc/cron.allow or /etc/cron.deny existed, and opsadmin user did not exist","Created opsadmin user (locked password, home dir) on node1","Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing exactly 'root' and 'opsadmin', root:root owned, mode 644; removed any stray /etc/cron.deny","Verified root and opsadmin can use crontab (list and install a job), then cleaned up the test job","Created and used a throwaway low-priv test user to confirm crontab denies non-listed users, then deleted that test user","Captured pre-restart boot_id and cron/cron.allow/opsadmin state as baseline","Issued a native reboot on node1 (single node) with acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec was available again and confirmed boot_id changed, proving an actual restart","Re-verified post-restart: cron service active, /etc/cron.allow and opsadmin persisted, opsadmin allowed, a fresh ephemeral test user denied, then removed that test user"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: no pre-existing cron.allow/cron.deny, opsadmin absent","command_ids":["cmd-97a26faa3e8a40f3"],"summary":"Confirmed /etc/cron.allow and /etc/cron.deny did not exist and opsadmin user did not exist prior to changes"},{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs","command_ids":["cmd-277f88d872df42bd","cmd-7db37a932bf1403e"],"summary":"Created /etc/cron.allow with root and opsadmin; demonstrated root and opsadmin can use crontab (list/install job) while a non-listed test user (crontest) is explicitly denied with 'You (crontest) are not allowed to use this program (crontab)'; cleaned up test user and temp job"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline (boot identity + service health) for node1","command_ids":["cmd-c1f2c0009ce34831"],"summary":"Captured boot_id f9bf293d-1eb8-423e-b185-84e94db646f3, cron service active, cron.allow contents, and opsadmin existence before restart"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-47a4b27c28c94cd9"],"summary":"Issued native 'reboot' via backgrounded sudo command; 'reboot-acknowledged' returned to the caller before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Proof of actual restart via changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-8070961b414649b2","cmd-3c66ada1cbf744d3"],"summary":"Connection reset confirmed the node went down; subsequent poll succeeded with boot_id changed to 72810ce8-b39f-4307-a33a-450cd2387bf3 and new uptime, proving a real reboot occurred"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of cron service, cron.allow restriction, and opsadmin account","command_ids":["cmd-8f6f813b43564c24"],"summary":"After restart, cron service active, /etc/cron.allow still contains root/opsadmin, opsadmin account persists and can use crontab, and a freshly created ephemeral test user is still denied by crontab (then removed), confirming the restriction survived the restart"}]},"ttft_ms":4565,"type":"result","duration_ms":69385,"uuid":"a8103583-16fb-46da-ad96-8cb8a253322d","ttft_stream_ms":2100,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":2100,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
